  "notes": "Inputs 1-2 are front combo XLR/jack (mic, line, instrument). Line Inputs 3-6 are rear jacks. Line Outputs 1-2 are the main speaker outputs, 3-4 the Alt pair. The guide's front panel description mentions up to two headphones, the specifications list one headphone output; one is listed here. Optical In/Out carry ADAT (8 ch at 44.1/48 kHz). Optional power inputs and the Kensington lock are not listed. Routing: inputs reach the computer via USB and the outputs via the Focusrite Control 2 mixer; computer playback reaches all outputs. Corrected: two headphone outputs (the user guide: 'Connect up to two sets of headphones'). Controls from the user guide, 'Front Panel': gain for inputs 1-2, 48V per input, INST (inputs 1 and 2 take instruments), AIR, SAFE, ALT (switches between monitor pairs 1-2 and 3-4), MUTE, main output level and two headphone levels. The INST, AIR, SAFE and 48V buttons act on the input chosen with SELECT and are shown once per input; AUTO (Auto Gain) is a one-shot function and not shown. Modelled: MUTE or ALT silence outputs 1 and 2. Assumption: levels at MIN are silent.",
